K4 tetrahedron with the transitive Klein group V4 = {e,(01)(23),(02)(13),(03)(12)}
  (1, 0, 3, 2): fixed vertices []; fixed distinguishable mixed pair (0, 1)-average vs (2, 3)-average
  (2, 3, 0, 1): fixed vertices []; fixed distinguishable mixed pair (0, 2)-average vs (1, 3)-average
  (3, 2, 1, 0): fixed vertices []; fixed distinguishable mixed pair (0, 3)-average vs (1, 2)-average
  -> transitive, every law fixes a distinguishable (mixed) pair, no law except e fixes a pure state.
